## 14. Classification

**CWE-640 – Weak Password Recovery Mechanism for Forgotten Password**

The vulnerability also involves improper trust in HTTP host information and can be categorized as a **Host Header Injection** leading to password reset poisoning.

---

## 15. Conclusion

The application contains a password reset poisoning vulnerability caused by trusting an attacker-controlled `Host` header.

An attacker can manipulate the hostname used in password reset emails, causing the reset link to point to an attacker-controlled server. When the victim follows the link, the password reset token is disclosed to the attacker.

The stolen token can subsequently be used to reset the victim's password and gain unauthorized access to the account.

In the laboratory environment, this technique successfully resulted in **full account takeover of the `carlos` user**.
